WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.360
- So you open up in the book

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.440
about like speaking of being
personal from the beginning.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.250
That's what I loved about
how raw and real you are,

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.170
'cause I feel like sometimes
that's few and far between

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.310
with people in the public eye.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.710
But you had to make an impossible decision

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:13.910
during a pregnancy.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.360
And I have known people, that
have had the same scenario.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.040
So what happened, you
know with the situation?

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.180
How did you cope with it?

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.960
'Cause that's a big
thing, to open up about.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.150
- Well what's interesting is that

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.710
when we had to make a
decision because we found out,

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.850
once we got into the second
trimester right away.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.510
Which usually, you know
once you get into that,

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:35.980
you're like "I'm in the clear."

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.100
- Yeah.
- But we found out

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.850
when we were into our second trimester

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.793
that there were some pretty
devastating health problems.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.360
And that the baby was
at risk, I was at risk.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.830
The baby probably wouldn't survive

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.610
and then I was at risk
for carrying any longer.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.090
And we really weren't in a position to,

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:54.180
the writing was on the wall,

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.703
there was nothing we could do.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.600
And my husband and I often say

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.510
that was the worst day of our lives.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.290
Making that decision.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.267
And--

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.970
Once I went through it,

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.160
I was really mad at my body and myself.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.790
Like I thought I did
something to cause it.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:14.750
Which I didn't.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.750
I didn't.
- Yeah.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.500
- You know but, you
just are trying so hard

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.130
to find an answer.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.660
And I found that once I went through that,

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.410
I started finding out
about these other women

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.040
who have gone through similar losses.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.160
And nobody was talking about it.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.500
- Yeah.
- But I felt that it was

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.530
really important to write about it,

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:36.400
because I wanted other people
to be able to feel safe

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.110
to share their story.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.430
And the fact that I wrote about it,

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.480
I can't tell you how many
people have reached out.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.970
- I can't imagine.
- Explaining how much

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.830
it's helped them and now they're able

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:49.240
to vocalize what they went through,

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.260
or they feel seen and heard.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.990
And, it's something that, was
really hard for me to share,

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.730
but I'm so glad I did
because it really helped

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.280
again build this community,

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.860
and made it safe for people to talk about.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.690
- Yeah and I'm one who loves therapy.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.710
So it just is sometimes
like learning and therapy--

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.740
Like just saying it out loud,

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.880
helps you heal.
- Right.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.460
- Like just saying it out
loud and not keeping it inside

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.960
and it just kind of building up.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.700
Like, saying it out loud
helps the person saying it.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.650
Just as much as somebody
connecting to the message

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:20.550
and feeling the same way.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.700
So it's very brave and it's very cool

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.353
and you're a very strong woman.

